1
00:01:33,650 --> 00:01:39,410
The Cursed Head

2
00:02:24,210 --> 00:02:26,600
Okay, here we go.

3
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,750
Ready, push!

4
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:50,900
Yes! That's the last one!

5
00:03:03,360 --> 00:03:06,160
I don't believe it.

6
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:09,540
It really was possible.

7
00:03:09,540 --> 00:03:12,610
Together, we turned an
entire forest into a farm.

8
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:17,510
Yeah, I think it took more than three years.

9
00:03:18,680 --> 00:03:22,390
If only all this land were ours.

10
00:03:23,670 --> 00:03:26,680
That's one thing a slave can't have.

11
00:03:29,570 --> 00:03:33,840
We worked hard. We're nearly there.

12
00:03:34,900 --> 00:03:39,190
Yeah. The other day, Pater told me something.

13
00:03:40,740 --> 00:03:46,740
We'll be able to buy our freedom with the
next harvest from this cleared land.

14
00:03:47,670 --> 00:03:49,940
We'll get some change back, too.

15
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:53,140
I see.

16
00:03:56,290 --> 00:04:01,190
Einar, what are you going to do
once you're a free man?

17
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:09,140
I don't know. Even if I went back to my homeland,
there's no family waiting for me.

18
00:04:10,310 --> 00:04:11,600
And besides...

19
00:04:13,330 --> 00:04:15,190
You're worried about Arnheid.

20
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:18,530
Yeah, I feel awkward about it.

21
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:24,240
If only Arnheid could be free, too.

22
00:04:25,090 --> 00:04:29,430
Then I'd feel better.

23
00:04:31,750 --> 00:04:35,780
The master has no intention
of letting her go.

24
00:04:39,310 --> 00:04:41,060
What about you, Thorfinn?

25
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:44,770
Will you go back to Iceland?

26
00:04:46,790 --> 00:04:51,020
Yeah. I think so. Probably.

27
00:04:51,460 --> 00:04:55,400
Seriously? You don't seem sure
about your plans.

28
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,930
Neither do you.

29
00:05:01,770 --> 00:05:05,400
Good grief. It's strange, isn't it?

30
00:05:06,210 --> 00:05:10,580
Freedom's just around the corner,
and we're acting like this.

31
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:25,430
There is something I'd like to try to do.

32
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:30,370
Really? What is it?

33
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:36,080
Well, there's a lot I'm still not sure about.

34
00:05:42,790 --> 00:05:45,410
What do you think, Einar?

35
00:05:48,270 --> 00:05:54,910
Would it be possible to rid the
world of war and slavery?

36
00:06:10,400 --> 00:06:14,530
Well... that would be like a dream.

37
00:06:22,710 --> 00:06:27,340
Ah, you've finally felled the last tree.

38
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:29,780
Well done, both of you.

39
00:06:30,250 --> 00:06:31,330
Master!

40
00:06:31,910 --> 00:06:36,570
Well? Do you think you'll be able
to till the soil in time for planting?

41
00:06:36,570 --> 00:06:38,850
Yes, probably, if we hurry.

42
00:06:41,910 --> 00:06:46,580
I see, I see. All right.
Then I'll give you a little discount.

43
00:06:47,970 --> 00:06:52,480
Once you're done sowing the seeds,
the two of you will be free.

44
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:58,690
You've worked hard, Thorfinn, Einar.

45
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:09,300
What? You don't seem that happy.

46
00:07:09,300 --> 00:07:11,100
Huh? What?

47
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:12,680
No! Wait, no!

48
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:14,930
All right!

49
00:07:15,510 --> 00:07:18,200
Thorfinn, we finally did it!

50
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:20,700
Y-Yeah!

51
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:24,630
Wait, sorry. Don't celebrate yet.

52
00:07:24,630 --> 00:07:25,280
What?

53
00:07:25,710 --> 00:07:29,750
You'll have to wait until after I return.

54
00:07:29,750 --> 00:07:32,180
You're going somewhere?

55
00:07:32,180 --> 00:07:36,970
Yes. By the way,
have you seen the old master?

56
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:39,620
He hasn't been this way.

57
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:44,470
I see. Maybe he's on his farm.

58
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,610
Well, you'll do.

59
00:07:47,610 --> 00:07:49,940
If you see him, give him this message.

60
00:07:51,050 --> 00:07:57,460
Tell him I've gone to the palace
in Jelling to visit King Harald.

61
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:01,790
I'm sure I'll be back in time
for planting, though.

62
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:05,470
Make sure you till the soil by then.

63
00:08:05,470 --> 00:08:06,320
Yes, sir.

64
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:10,690
Safe travels.

65
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:13,920
Oh, right.

66
00:08:14,950 --> 00:08:21,890
How would you like to continue working
for me as my retainers once you're free?

67
00:08:22,390 --> 00:08:25,860
I'd gladly welcome a couple of
hard workers like you.

68
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:30,020
Give it some thought.

69
00:08:46,290 --> 00:08:56,290
What benefit is there for the worker from that
in which he labors? I have seen the task which
God has given the sons of mankind with which
to occupy themselves. He has made everything
appropriate in its time.

70
00:08:55,010 --> 00:09:05,010
He has also set eternity in their heart, without the
possibility that mankind will find out the work
which God has done from the beginning even
to the end.

71
00:09:01,640 --> 00:09:07,770
Ecclesiastes 3:9-11

72
00:09:34,370 --> 00:09:36,560
Excuse me, Your Majesty.

73
00:09:37,810 --> 00:09:41,180
Our ship will be arriving in Jelling shortly.

74
00:09:41,870 --> 00:09:45,190
Please wake up, King Canute.

75
00:10:30,590 --> 00:10:34,790
Your Majesty, what are you doing out here?

76
00:10:34,790 --> 00:10:36,740
Our horses will be ready soon.

77
00:10:36,740 --> 00:10:38,160
Please wait inside your cabin.

78
00:10:38,680 --> 00:10:39,680
Here is fine.

79
00:10:41,360 --> 00:10:43,090
I haven't been back home in a while.

80
00:10:43,610 --> 00:10:44,930
I want to feel the breeze.

81
00:10:47,920 --> 00:10:49,090
Your Majesty.

82
00:10:52,610 --> 00:10:56,630
I am delighted to see you've
safely returned from England.

83
00:10:56,630 --> 00:11:01,300
Thank you. Wulf, how is my brother doing?

84
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:02,320
My liege.

85
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:06,270
King Harald is not well.

86
00:11:06,860 --> 00:11:09,450
His pain has worsened over the past month.

87
00:11:09,450 --> 00:11:13,700
He's no longer capable of speaking.

88
00:11:15,410 --> 00:11:18,940
I see. How much longer does he have?

89
00:11:19,620 --> 00:11:25,310
According to those treating him,
these next few days will be critical.

90
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:31,860
Very well. Thank you for
watching over him in my place.

91
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:32,710
Yes, Your Majesty.

92
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:38,470
Ouch.

93
00:11:38,470 --> 00:11:40,230
I won again.

94
00:11:39,590 --> 00:11:41,440
That ball game they're playing...

95
00:11:40,230 --> 00:11:41,700
Are you okay?

96
00:11:40,590 --> 00:11:41,890
Again.

97
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:43,470
Don't hurt yourself.

98
00:11:42,430 --> 00:11:46,850
My brother was quite good at it
when we were children.

99
00:11:43,710 --> 00:11:45,070
Darn you.

100
00:11:50,430 --> 00:11:53,940
He occasionally played with me.

101
00:11:58,690 --> 00:12:00,850
Harald, hit it again.

102
00:12:03,170 --> 00:12:06,230
Okay. Watch the ball closely, Canute.

103
00:12:07,090 --> 00:12:10,780
Those within the palace
feuded amongst themselves

104
00:12:10,780 --> 00:12:13,920
over which of us would succeed our father,

105
00:12:14,730 --> 00:12:18,990
but my brother never paid
any heed to it himself.

106
00:12:19,860 --> 00:12:20,790
Ready?

107
00:12:21,690 --> 00:12:22,690
Here it comes.

108
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:29,980
Your Highness!

109
00:12:29,980 --> 00:12:30,790
Ragnar...

110
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:41,960
I'm okay.

111
00:12:41,960 --> 00:12:43,310
I don't believe it.

112
00:12:44,550 --> 00:12:48,290
See? He's tougher than you think.

113
00:12:48,850 --> 00:12:53,190
You're a little too overprotective,
you know. You should—

114
00:12:53,190 --> 00:12:54,800
Impressive, Your Highness.

115
00:12:58,630 --> 00:13:00,220
I knew you could do it.

116
00:13:00,220 --> 00:13:02,620
Are you certain you're not hurt?

117
00:13:02,620 --> 00:13:04,960
Yeah. Thanks, Ragnar.

118
00:13:06,310 --> 00:13:09,320
But it's hard to move when
I'm wearing so many layers.

119
00:13:09,320 --> 00:13:11,850
I'm hot, too. Can I take these off?

120
00:13:11,850 --> 00:13:13,430
No.

121
00:13:13,940 --> 00:13:18,070
A warrior must be properly equipped.

122
00:13:18,070 --> 00:13:20,440
Are you listening, Your Highness?

123
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:25,930
Letting your guard down for even
a moment can prove fatal.

124
00:13:22,370 --> 00:13:25,930
He was a strong, kind man.

125
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,080
Even I once...

126
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:32,990
My brother helped me often.

127
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,630
I must thank him.

128
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:40,390
Hup!

129
00:13:56,250 --> 00:13:59,060
Play somewhere else, children.

130
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:01,110
Sorry.

131
00:14:08,750 --> 00:14:10,780
Don't hit it so hard, Asta.

132
00:14:10,780 --> 00:14:13,240
Hmph. You're just slow.

133
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:14,880
Unbelievable. Children are so carefree.

134
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:14,860
What did you say?

135
00:14:15,950 --> 00:14:17,460
Now you're mad.

136
00:14:16,670 --> 00:14:18,670
What is the matter, Your Majesty?

137
00:14:24,340 --> 00:14:25,710
It's nothing.

138
00:14:31,150 --> 00:14:38,020
Sweyn's sons inherited their own
respective territories from their father.

139
00:14:39,330 --> 00:14:41,970
The older brother Harald inherited Denmark,

140
00:14:42,540 --> 00:14:45,540
and the younger brother Canute
inherited England.

141
00:14:46,120 --> 00:14:48,880
Their relationship was good.

142
00:14:50,990 --> 00:14:54,140
During Canute's conquest of England,

143
00:14:54,140 --> 00:15:00,740
his brother Harald directly supported him
by sending a fleets of ships.

144
00:15:01,650 --> 00:15:02,720
However...

145
00:15:03,980 --> 00:15:10,950
Shortly after Canute became
King of England, Harald fell ill.

146
00:15:12,190 --> 00:15:15,490
Harald had no heirs.

147
00:15:18,340 --> 00:15:20,020
Brother Canute!

148
00:15:20,020 --> 00:15:23,410
You really did come to Jelling.

149
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:26,790
Address me as "Your Majesty," Estrid.

150
00:15:26,790 --> 00:15:29,780
Your visit is so sudden. I was surprised.

151
00:15:32,450 --> 00:15:36,270
It's good to see you again, King Harald.

152
00:15:41,350 --> 00:15:45,860
Brother Harald,
Brother Canute has come to visit you.

153
00:15:46,590 --> 00:15:48,320
Can you tell he's here?

154
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:52,050
It's fine. You don't have to wake him.

155
00:15:52,440 --> 00:15:53,890
I'll be staying here a while.

156
00:15:54,310 --> 00:15:57,730
I'll speak to His Majesty
when he's feeling better.

157
00:15:59,940 --> 00:16:02,390
Canute...

158
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:15,150
King Harald, I am here.

159
00:16:17,500 --> 00:16:19,570
Please rest.

160
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:24,550
You needn't worry about your kingdom.

161
00:16:28,630 --> 00:16:32,470
I've been waiting for you.

162
00:16:34,500 --> 00:16:36,650
Denmark...

163
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:45,480
Denmark is yours.

164
00:16:52,100 --> 00:16:55,570
Don't be absurd, King Harald.

165
00:16:56,180 --> 00:17:00,910
Get well soon so we can play ball again.

166
00:17:02,120 --> 00:17:05,750
You've got some guts, Canute.

167
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:11,380
I'm impressed you can lie about that
like you don't know what's going on.

168
00:17:14,180 --> 00:17:15,170
Brother?

169
00:17:16,930 --> 00:17:21,110
You're visiting the man
you poisoned yourself?

170
00:17:21,110 --> 00:17:29,150
What a farce. What will you
accomplish by doing that?

171
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:34,790
Harald was friendly to you.

172
00:17:34,790 --> 00:17:38,160
Why did you need to kill him?

173
00:17:38,160 --> 00:17:42,210
You could've ruled the world together.

174
00:17:43,460 --> 00:17:47,290
You didn't do it for the sake of
peace and prosperity.

175
00:17:47,940 --> 00:17:52,660
Ambition now rests within your heart.

176
00:17:53,130 --> 00:17:58,850
The ambition to rule as
king of all the North Sea.

177
00:18:02,340 --> 00:18:08,590
That is the curse. The crown's curse.

178
00:18:09,940 --> 00:18:12,900
None can escape it.

179
00:18:14,390 --> 00:18:23,430
By donning the two crowns
of Denmark and England,

180
00:18:23,430 --> 00:18:28,110
you will suffer twice as much as I did.

181
00:18:36,550 --> 00:18:37,620
Brother!

182
00:18:44,660 --> 00:18:47,230
What's wrong? You suddenly went into a daze.

183
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:49,990
Have you fallen ill, too?

184
00:19:00,390 --> 00:19:03,890
I'm fine. I just felt a little dizzy.

185
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:10,080
Prepare a bedchamber.

186
00:19:10,440 --> 00:19:12,690
His Majesty is tired from
his long voyage at sea.

187
00:19:43,850 --> 00:19:44,590
What is it?

188
00:19:45,020 --> 00:19:48,820
Lady Estrid instructed me
to bring you something to drink.

189
00:19:50,870 --> 00:19:52,620
Where did it come from?

190
00:19:53,220 --> 00:19:56,500
What? Where is it from?

191
00:19:58,850 --> 00:20:02,010
I don't need any. I'm not thirsty.

192
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:08,770
You fear being poisoned
because you poison others.

193
00:20:09,430 --> 00:20:12,080
Isn't that right, Canute?

194
00:20:17,460 --> 00:20:23,610
It was rather mischievous of you to appear
in the middle of the afternoon, King Sweyn.

195
00:20:24,150 --> 00:20:32,120
If you can see me during the day,
then the curse must be growing stronger.

196
00:20:33,230 --> 00:20:34,500
Is he talking to himself?

197
00:20:35,280 --> 00:20:37,280
How long are you going to
keep standing there?

198
00:20:37,280 --> 00:20:39,210
I need nothing from you. Leave.

199
00:20:39,210 --> 00:20:41,170
Y-Yes, Your Majesty!

200
00:20:44,230 --> 00:20:48,240
Uniting the nation is
essential to creating a utopia.

201
00:20:48,860 --> 00:20:52,590
Two kings would eventually cause trouble.

202
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:56,050
King Harald's death is necessary.

203
00:21:00,290 --> 00:21:02,780
I'm surprised.

204
00:21:03,240 --> 00:21:10,030
You've come to think
like a real king, Canute.

205
00:21:15,750 --> 00:21:17,870
What are you laughing about?

206
00:21:19,190 --> 00:21:25,060
King Sweyn, I once hated you
and wished for your death.

207
00:21:25,780 --> 00:21:27,680
But now?

208
00:21:28,750 --> 00:21:33,470
You're the only one I can speak to frankly.

209
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:38,270
Let us be friends,

210
00:21:40,820 --> 00:21:43,920
as befits two cursed men.

211
00:21:57,440 --> 00:21:59,650
Brother, again!

212
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:04,030
Okay.

213
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:07,580
Here it comes, Canute.

214
00:22:07,580 --> 00:22:08,350
Okay.

215
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:10,000
Harald.

216
00:22:14,160 --> 00:22:16,980
We're holding a war council. Join us.

217
00:22:18,360 --> 00:22:19,670
Yes, Father.

218
00:22:22,110 --> 00:22:23,780
Sorry, Canute.

219
00:22:24,270 --> 00:22:25,650
We'll continue another time.

220
00:22:28,270 --> 00:22:29,870
Thank you, Brother.

221
00:22:47,140 --> 00:22:49,890
Grow up strong, Canute.

222
00:22:51,730 --> 00:22:54,550
Stronger than me and father.

223
00:22:56,190 --> 00:22:57,040
Got it?

224
00:23:00,670 --> 00:23:01,380
Yes.

225
00:23:22,060 --> 00:23:26,310
Come, Your Highness.
I'll be your next opponent.

226
00:23:26,310 --> 00:23:28,570
What? Can you even play, Ragnar?

227
00:23:28,570 --> 00:23:30,550
How dare you.

228
00:23:30,550 --> 00:23:36,070
I was once feared as Gullinbursti of the Lake,
and for seven consecutive years...

229
00:23:45,890 --> 00:23:47,410
Is this all there is to it?

230
00:23:50,740 --> 00:23:52,770
This is nothing.

231
00:25:36,470 --> 00:25:39,930
Kings and Swords

232
00:25:37,640 --> 00:25:39,170
"Kings and Swords."
